    "description": "CCSWE design tokens — single source of truth for the marketing site (web) and the Android system (Jetpack Compose / Material 3). M3-anchored core: M3 ColorScheme roles, M3 type scale (15 roles), M3 shape scale, M3 motion scale (10 durations + 6 easings). Consumer-shaped translation lives in `tokens.web.json` (web) and `tokens.local.json` (Android).",
    "schemes": ["dark", "light", "darkHighContrast", "lightHighContrast"],
    "notes": [
      "Values are unitless integers. Convention: 1 = 1dp on Android = 1sp on Android (for type) = 1/16 rem on web. At default density / default browser zoom these resolve to identical physical sizes.",
      "Per-role `letterSpacing` is in em (relative), not the unitless dp/sp scale. M3 defines it that way; Android multiplies by sp at apply time, web emits as em directly.",
      "This file is M3-anchored: M3 ColorScheme roles, M3 type scale (15 roles), M3 shape scale, M3 motion scale (10 durations + 6 easings). No spacing — spacing has no standard M3 category and surface needs don't generalize. Spacing lives in `tokens.web.json` (web) and `tokens.local.json` (Android).",
      "No CSS-shaped fields here: no rem strings, no `ms` suffixes, no font-stack strings, no `cubic-bezier(...)` strings, no box-shadow strings, no gradient strings. Composition into CSS is the web layer's job.",
      "`typography.fontFamily.<name>` is now structured: `{ googleName, loadedWeights }`. `googleName` is the family identifier as used by Google Fonts and CSS `font-family` literals. `loadedWeights` documents the weight set that consumers' default font-loading strategy (`tokens.fonts.css` or equivalent) ships — synthesizing weights outside this set produces fake-bold/fake-italic rendering.",
      "Primitive ramps `surface` and `onSurface` are the Tailwind slate and gray scales respectively. Splitting them lets a scheme keep slate-tinted containers while body text and outlines pull from a true neutral.",
      "The semantic layer encodes the M3 ColorScheme contract. Any value with `ref` resolves to a primitive at build time. Any value with `value` is a tuned hex used directly — these are reserved for the surface elevation ladder where exact ramp steps don't exist (e.g. `surfaceContainer` between 800 and 900).",
      "Light, dark-HC, and light-HC schemes are encoded for Android. The web layer ships dark by default and exposes the others under `[data-theme=...]` selectors so a site can opt in later.",
      "Brand triad container/onContainer values (e.g. `primaryContainer`) are tuned for dark, derived for light. They live on the brand layer rather than the neutral ramp.",
      "`onSurfaceStrong` is a stronger-emphasis sibling of `onSurface` for headings and callout text that need a brightness step. M3-aligned conceptually but not part of the canonical M3 ColorScheme. Resolves brighter on dark, darker on light, mirroring `onSurface` itself."
    ]
  },

